lt;/span&gt;' style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=5;spacingBottom=5;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1935" y="335" width="290" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dep-o_news" value='&lt;b style="font-size:12px"&gt;Google News&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11px"&gt;news.google.com/rss/search&lt;/span&gt;' style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=5;spacingBottom=5;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1935" y="395" width="290" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dep-o_le" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;Let's Encrypt&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;issues and renews Caddy's certificate&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=5;spacingBottom=5;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1935" y="455" width="290" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dep-p_light" value='&lt;b style="font-size:12px"&gt;Planned, not done: move to AWS Lightsail&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11px"&gt;small_3_1: 2 vCPU, 2 GB RAM, 60 GB SSD, Debian 13, $12 a month flat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11px"&gt;ports 22, 80, 443 only; 3000 and 8000 closed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11px"&gt;the plan is aditya/lightsail-migration.md, 27 Sep&lt;/span&gt;' style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#999999;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=5;spacingBottom=5;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1A1A1A;dashed=1;dashPattern=6 4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="657" width="700" height="75" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dep-p_cost" value='&lt;b style="font-size:12px"&gt;Cost rule&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11px"&gt;the EC2 box is stopped when nobody is working on it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11px"&gt;stopped: about $8 a month (disk and idle Elastic IP) · running all month: about $139&lt;/span&gt;' style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=5;spacingBottom=5;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="750" y="657" width="600" height="61" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dep-p_redeploy" value='&lt;b style="font-size:12px"&gt;Redeploying after a merge (aditya/server.md)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11px"&gt;build main on the Mac first, so a broken build never reaches the box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11px"&gt;ssh indra → stop indra-api → git pull --ff-only → alembic upgrade head → start → curl /healthz&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11px"&gt;rebuild the dashboard with the HTTPS API base, then restart indra-frontend&lt;/span&gt;' style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=5;spacingBottom=5;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1380" y="657" width="860" height="75" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dep-e1" value="HTTPS 443" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;endSize=7;strokeColor=#555555;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=10;fontColor=#333333;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;jumpStyle=arc;jumpSize=8;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.2103;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="dep-u_cit" target="dep-n_sg"><mxGeometry rela